Entity Collision FPS Fix (Itamio port for Minecraft 26.3)

This mod is an unofficial port of "Entity Collision FPS Fix" by CorgiTaco
(and jklw10), published on Modrinth
(https://modrinth.com/mod/entity-collision-fps-fix).

Original source: https://github.com/CorgiTaco/No-Client-Side-Entity-Collision-Checks
Original license: CC0-1.0 (see LICENSE, preserved from the original project).

The original mod removes client-side entity collision checks (Entity.isInWall
for Entity and LivingEntity, and LivingEntity.pushEntities on the client),
which boosts FPS and works around Mojang bug MC-228976 (client-side entity
collision checks running on the render thread).

All credit for the original concept, design, and logic goes to CorgiTaco and
the original authors. This port was created by Itamio to bring the
functionality to Minecraft 26.3 (Fabric) because the original mod has not
been updated to this version.

Itamio does not take credit for any of the original assets or logic.
The code was updated to be compatible with Minecraft 26.3 (Fabric), where
Entity.level is a level() accessor and Level.isClientSide is an
isClientSide() method.
